{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/design/spec/context-chronology-profile-v1.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Context, chronology, and resolution profile v1\n\nThis bounded profile implements P06 engineering behaviour for exact rational\nquantities, Gregorian half-open dates, finite populations, and nonnegative\nunhedged bullet debt. It is a versioned runtime contract, not an accounting\neligibility or forecast-validity claim.\n\n## Public operations\n\n`Context` identifies concept, entity, perimeter and version, basis, measurement,\nunit/currency, calendar, dimensions, and gross/net status. `compatible_context`\nrequires all fields to match or an explicit dated `MappingRule`; parent/group,\nperimeter, basis, measurement, currency, calendar, dimension, and gross/net\nmismatches are rejected. Mapping cycles, expired rules, and unsupported conversion\nkinds fail with stable diagnostic codes.\n\n`check_partition` independently checks finite member sets. Members must be disjoint\nand cover the declared population, or an explicitly named residual must be present;\nan unknown residual cannot produce an exact total. Population and axis signatures\nprevent combining alternative classifications.\n\n`select_evidence` validates a supersession DAG and filters assertions by filing\navailability and optional ingestion cutoff before selecting `original`,\n`latest_available`, or `harmonised`. Date-only availability requires an explicit\nnamed timezone and `next_local_midnight` policy. Unknown retained-byte vintage is\nreturned as unresolved. Harmonisation preserves source IDs and transformation\nprovenance.\n\n`subtract_cumulative` computes an exact scalar flow only when concept, context,\ncalendar, start, nested exclusive ends, and revision compatibility agree. It\nrejects instant values and incompatible vintages; reviewed exceptions must name\nscope and evidence.\n\n`admit_uncertainty` supports exactly six categories: ExtractionReading,\nHistoricalFact, AccountingElection, MeasurementEstimate, BehaviourPolicy, and\nFutureInnovation. It validates dependencies and category-specific fields. Unknown\ncategories, unsupported methods/treatments, invalid finite joint laws, and\nincompatible measures fail explicitly.\n\n`resolve_bullet_debt` retains constituents and validates a query signature over\ncontract, context, evidence view, horizon, scenario, requested outputs, and accrual\nconvention. Any changed signature requires fresh validation. The supported exact\ncase is fixed-rate unhedged bullet debt with no maturity crossing. The optional\nfixed-rate approximation requires nonnegative horizon, a declared tolerance, and a\ncertificate using the triangle inequality:\n`|sum(P_i r_i T)-sum(P_i) r* T| <= T sum(P_i |r_i-r*|)`.\n\n## Evidence and default audit\n\n| Choice | Provenance | Failure mode | Smallest diagnostic | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Exact `Fraction` arithmetic | Core 0 and P03 rational helpers | float rounding changes subtraction or bounds | independent Fraction oracle | reviewed bounded default |\n| Gregorian half-open dates | Core 0 temporal fixture | inclusive end or calendar mismatch | nested interval tests | reviewed bounded default |\n| Date-only next-local-midnight | approved P06 plan | UTC/local boundary selects wrong assertion | named-zone boundary test | explicit policy |\n| Finite partition populations | approved P06 plan | proof string hides overlap or omission | set enumeration | convenience test input |\n| Six uncertainty categories | P03 admission fields and approved plan | malformed evidence admitted | positive plus semantic negative per category | bounded support |\n| Bullet-debt grouping | P04 additive reference and approved plan | stale/query-insufficient grouping | query signature and constituent oracle | bounded hypothesis |\n| Approximation certificate | approved plan derivation | tolerance claimed without error bound | exact difference versus bound | optional reviewed path |\n\nSynthetic fixtures test structure only. P01 source records with\n`historical_byte_vintage=not_established_by_this_inventory` remain unresolved for\nhistorical byte selection. Passing this profile does not establish professional\naccounting treatment, empirical forecast validity, or human acceptance.\n\n## Criterion map\n\nMC02: numeric context; MC05: chronology and YTD; MC06: perimeter rejection;\nMC07: mappings and partitions; MC10: category admission; MC11: query-dependent\ngrouping and approximation; MC14: information dates and scenario semantics. Tests in `tests/test_accounting_p06.py` provide independent expected\nsets and arithmetic.\n\n## Repair audit and executable scope\n\nThe recovery audit rejected field-presence checks as evidence of semantic admission.\nIt also found that selected source values did not drive the integrated calculation.\nThe repaired tests use independent rational/set oracles, reference resolution,\ncutoff boundaries, invalid inputs and source-value/revision-link mutations.\nA failing invariant requires repair; missing provenance, changed protected inputs,\nor invalid test execution prevents a passing report. No ranking or scientific\nexperiment is performed. Conformance and result files preserve actual checks.\n\nContext records require explicit Gregorian calendars and immutable dimensions.\nComponent and reclassification operations enumerate atomic population values with\none contribution per member. Combining two complete axes over the same population\nis rejected. Identity harmonisation creates a new observation with the original\nvalue, source and dependency; all numerical harmonisations are unsupported.\nUnknown retained-byte availability is visible as unresolved and excluded by the\nintegrated entrypoint. Low-level selection defaults to assertion chronology;\n`require_known_bytes=True` requests the stricter historical-byte view.\n\nAdmission resolves source/locator, accepted evidence, dated package permission and\neligibility, finite historical domains and evidence bounds, measurement input\navailability and method-specific inputs, dated policy information and complete\nfinite joint laws. Supported estimate operations are direct/observable values and\nsingle-cash-flow DCF with integer nonnegative years. Only a hold behaviour policy\nis implemented. These restrictions are explicit rejection boundaries, not general\naccounting defaults. Permissions and evidence assertions still require substantive\nreview; structural acceptance cannot establish their truth.\n\nFixed-rate debt uses exact principal-times-rate-times-horizon simple accrual. The\nhorizon is an explicitly supplied year fraction; no inherited day count is used.\nMaturity at or before the horizon, floating resets and hedges are unsupported.\nFresh grouping checks run after horizon, scenario, report or evidence changes.\nCached signatures include actual constituent values. The triangle bound follows\nfrom |T sum P_i(r_i-r*)| <= T sum P_i|r_i-r*| for P_i,T >= 0; it is recomputed\non every approximation request. A supplied signature must match; absent signatures\nrequest fresh certification, not reuse of prior error evidence. Exact outputs and\napproximate estimates are separately labelled.\n\nThe finite synthetic amounts and permissions are convenience inputs justified by\ntransparent arithmetic and controlled rejection cases. Their failure mode is a\nshared interpretation error; source and professional accounting validity remain\nunevaluated. P01 adapter preserves publication metadata without promoting filing\ndates to retained-byte availability. P03 adapters preserve literal/review metadata\nand require missing context supplements explicitly. Returned results are copied\nfrom engine state, and failed mutations are atomic.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
