0128dfb1976121620f5886116574beaf01\\\",\\n    \\\"approved_plan_hash\\\": \\\"e61663d39f7452b2c8baf92b4a7dfdd9e10cbea62c65d36ccb74481bee16cfe3\\\",\\n    \\\"execution_inventory\\\": \\\"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P06/execution-0/pre-edit-files.json\\\",\\n    \\\"outputs\\\": [\\n      \\\"data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06/conformance.json\\\",\\n      \\\"data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06/result.md\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"result\\\": \\\"data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06/result.md\\\",\\n    \\\"phase_contribution_files\\\": [\\n      \\\"scripts/context_chronology_v1.py\\\",\\n      \\\"scripts/check_accounting_p06.py\\\",\\n      \\\"tests/test_accounting_p06.py\\\",\\n      \\\"docs/design/spec/context-chronology-profile-v1.md\\\",\\n      \\\"docs/design/fixtures/p06-context-chronology-cases-v1.json\\\",\\n      \\\"data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06/conformance.json\\\",\\n      \\\"data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06/result.md\\\"\\n    ]\\n  }\\n}\\n# P06 context, chronology, and resolution result\\n\\nPASS: 18 P06 tests, 11 P03 regression tests, and 21 P04 regression tests executed. The conformance file records every test outcome, independent criterion probe, source hash, inventory comparison, command, and manifest.\\n\\nThe implementation supplies explicit context mappings, finite partition enumeration, supersession-DAG evidence selection, date-only next-local-midnight handling, revision-compatible YTD subtraction, six category-specific uncertainty admission, information-view guards, and query-signature-bound fixed-rate unhedged bullet-debt resolution. Exact Fraction arithmetic is used throughout the supported scalar path. An approximation is accepted only with a fixed-rate scope, declared tolerance, and a triangle-inequality error certificate.\\n\\nThe tests independently verify 260 minus revised H1 110 equals H2 150 and reject subtraction using incompatible original H1 120. They reject parent/group, basis, measurement, currency, calendar, gross/net, overlap, omission, dangling/cyclic revision, future-information, unsupported treatment, unsupported scenario, stale-query, maturity-crossing, and missing-approximation-evidence cases. Historical byte availability marked unknown remains unresolved in evidence output.\\n\\n| Decision | Primary criterion | Veto status | Main uncertainty | Next justified action | Not concluded |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| PASS for bounded engineering conformance | Independent P06 probes and focused/regression suites | tests=True; protection=True; stable=True; failed_observations=[] | finite synthetic cases and unannotated source availability | independent result review if PASS; repair if FAIL | professional accounting validity, empirical forecast validity, human acceptance, or wider MC01–MC35/G1–G18 closure |\\n\\nEngineering correctness, numerical validity, and interpretation remain separate. The exact outputs establish only the declared bounded operations. The strongest alternative explanation is a shared interpretation error in the synthetic fixtures; independent set and arithmetic probes reduce that risk but do not replace source or professional review. The weakest evidence is breadth: mappings, uncertainty, and grouping are finite bounded cases.\\n\\nResiduals: general measurement conversion, consolidation, arbitrary calendars, continuous or nonlinear uncertainty, empirical approximation validation, historical retained-byte availability, accounting validity, forecast validity, and human acceptance remain open. This phase does not rank stochastic candidates or establish a production default.\\n\\nActual command: `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python3 -B scripts/check_accounting_p06.py --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06 --approved-plan data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P06/approved-plan.json --execution-inventory data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P06/execution-0/pre-edit-files.json`. Python 3.11.15, CPU only with accelerator devices intentionally hidden. Wall time: 4.462378 seconds. Git provenance is unavailable; content hashes and supervisor inventories are retained in conformance.json.\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g 'CLAUDE.md' -g '*p06*' -g '*context-chronology*' -g '*context_chronology*'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g 'CLAUDE.md' -g '*p06*' -g '*context-chronology*' -g '*context_chronology*'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"scripts/__pycache__/check_accounting_p06.cpython-311.pyc\\nscripts/__pycache__/context_chronology_v1.cpython-311.pyc\\nscripts/check_accounting_p06.py\\nscripts/context_chronology_v1.py\\nAGENTS.md\\ntests/__pycache__/test_accounting_p06.cpython-311.pyc\\ntests/test_accounting_p06.py\\ndocs/design/review/pre-repair-2026-10-02/AGENTS.md\\ndocs/design/spec/context-chronology-profile-v1.md\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/AGENTS.md\\ndocs/design/fixtures/p06-context-chronology-cases-v1.json\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'wc -l AGENTS.md scripts/context_chronology_v1.py scripts/check_accounting_p06.py tests/test_accounting_p06.py docs/design/spec/context-chronology-profile-v1.md docs/design/fixtures/p06-context-chronology-cases-v1.json'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'wc -l AGENTS.md scripts/context_chronology_v1.py scripts/check_accounting_p06.py tests/test_accounting_p06.py docs/design/spec/context-chronology-profile-v1.md docs/design/fixtures/p06-context-chronology-cases-v1.json'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   58 AGENTS.md\\n  677 scripts/context_chronology_v1.py\\n  199 scripts/check_accounting_p06.py\\n  247 tests/test_accounting_p06.py\\n   70 docs/design/spec/context-chronology-profile-v1.md\\n   13 docs/design/fixtures/p06-context-chronology-cases-v1.json\\n 1264 total\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,180p' docs/design/spec/context-chronology-profile-v1.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,180p' docs/design/spec/context-chronology-profile-v1.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Context, chronology, and resolution profile v1\\n\\nThis bounded profile implements P06 engineering behaviour for exact rational\\nquantities, Gregorian half-open dates, finite populations, and nonnegative\\nunhedged bullet debt. It is a versioned runtime contract, not an accounting\\neligibility or forecast-validity claim.\\n\\n## Public operations\\n\\n`Context` identifies concept, entity, perimeter and version, basis, measurement,\\nunit/currency, calendar, dimensions, and gross/net status. `compatible_context`\\nrequires all fields to match or an explicit dated `MappingRule`; parent/group,\\nperimeter, basis, measurement, currency, calendar, dimension, and gross/net\\nmismatches are rejected. Mapping cycles, expired rules, and unsupported conversion\\nkinds fail with stable diagnostic codes.\\n\\n`check_partition` independently checks finite member sets. Members must be disjoint\\nand cover the declared population, or an explicitly named residual must be present;\\nan unknown residual cannot produce an exact total. Population and axis signatures\\nprevent combining alternative classifications.\\n\\n`select_evidence` validates a supersession DAG and filters assertions by filing\\navailability and optional ingestion cutoff before selecting `original`,\\n`latest_available`, or `harmonised`. Date-only availability requires an explicit\\nnamed timezone and `next_local_midnight` policy. Unknown retained-byte vintage is\\nreturned as unresolved. Harmonisation preserves source IDs and transformation\\nprovenance.\\n\\n`subtract_cumulative` computes an exact scalar flow only when concept, context,\\ncalendar, start, nested exclusive ends, and revision compatibility agree. It\\nrejects instant values and incompatible vintages; reviewed exceptions must name\\nscope and evidence.\\n\\n`admit_uncertainty` supports exactly six categories: ExtractionReading,\\nHistoricalFact, AccountingElection, MeasurementEstimate, BehaviourPolicy, and\\nFutureInnovation. It validates dependencies and category-specific fields. Unknown\\ncategories, unsupported methods/treatments, invalid finite joint laws, and\\nincompatible measures fail explicitly.\\n\\n`resolve_bullet_debt` retains constituents and validates a query signature over\\ncontract, context, evidence view, horizon, scenario, requested outputs, and accrual\\nconvention. Any changed signature requires fresh validation. The supported exact\\ncase is fixed-rate unhedged bullet debt with no maturity crossing. The optional\\nfixed-rate approximation requires nonnegative horizon, a declared tolerance, and a\\ncertificate using the triangle inequality:\\n`|sum(P_i r_i T)-sum(P_i) r* T| <= T sum(P_i |r_i-r*|)`.\\n\\n## Evidence and default audit\\n\\n| Choice | Provenance | Failure mode | Smallest diagnostic | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Exact `Fraction` arithmetic | Core 0 and P03 rational helpers | float rounding changes subtraction or bounds | independent Fraction oracle | reviewed bounded default |\\n| Gregorian half-open dates | Core 0 temporal fixture | inclusive end or calendar mismatch | nested interval tests | reviewed bounded default |\\n| Date-only next-local-midnight | approved P06 plan | UTC/local boundary selects wrong assertion | named-zone boundary test | explicit policy |\\n| Finite partition populations | approved P06 plan | proof string hides overlap or omission | set enumeration | convenience test input |\\n| Six uncertainty categories | P03 admission fields and approved plan | malformed evidence admitted | positive plus semantic negative per category | bounded support |\\n| Bullet-debt grouping | P04 additive reference and approved plan | stale/query-insufficient grouping | query signature and constituent oracle | bounded hypothesis |\\n| Approximation certificate | approved plan derivation | tolerance claimed without error bound | exact difference versus bound | optional reviewed path |\\n\\nSynthetic fixtures test structure only. P01 source records with\\n`historical_byte_vintage=not_established_by_this_inventory` remain unresolved for\\nhistorical byte selection. Passing this profile does not establish professional\\naccounting treatment, empirical forecast validity, or human acceptance.\\n\\n## Criterion map\\n\\nMC02/MC05: context and partition checks; MC06/MC07: chronology and YTD revision\\nselection; MC10: category admission; MC11/MC14: query-dependent grouping and\\napproximation. Tests in `tests/test_accounting_p06.py` provide independent expected\\nsets and arithmetic.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"rg -n '\\\"'^#|''^def |''^class |''^    def |''^@|MC02|MC05|MC06|MC07|MC10|MC11|MC14'\\\"' scripts/context_chronology_v1.py scripts/check_accounting_p06.py tests/test_accounting_p06.py AGENTS.md docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"i