 source-acquisition layer:\\n**192 of 192 target reports, 2018–2025, across nine issuers and three evidenced\\naccounting families. All nine have eight consecutive complete years.**\\n`target-panel-v2.json` is active and is now the collector's explicit default.\\nHenkel replaces Unilever and Munich Re replaces Allianz under the reviewed\\nsource-access repair; frozen v1 coverage and all original files remain under\\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/snapshots/`.\\n\\nResume from the [corpus result](accounting-benchmark-corpus-results.md),\\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/index.html`, `coverage.json` and\\n`integrity-manifest.json`. QA 6 revalidated all 244 retained original versions;\\nthe independent hash/provenance/grid/PDF checks pass, and 20 regression tests\\npass. T\\ndocs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md\\n# Accounting master checkpoint\\n\\nUpdated 3 October 2026, Hong Kong, during run `20261002T233421-cea9e631`.\\nThe user's create/review/execute instruction and original standing grant remain\\nactive. The catalog preserves all MC01–MC35 and G1–G18, with no missing IDs.\\n\\n## Active run and next action\\n\\nTool session `78463` is running. P00–P04 are accepted internally; P05 is\\nplanning. Do not launch another master or edit controller files while it is\\nactive. Poll the session and consult current state before resuming. This is\\na dated checkpoint; saved state and events record subsequent changes.\\n\\n```text\\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py status\\n```\\n\\nAfter this invocation exits, resume with:\\n\\n```text\\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py run\\n```\\n\\nThe current invocation has the configured 7,200-second wall limit, sequential\\nworkers and bounded repair attempts. A budget boundary retains partial work\\nand the next plan; it does not complete the mission.\\n\\n- [State](../../data/accounting-master/state.json)\\n- [Next plan](../../data/accounting-master/next-plan.md)\\n- [Events](../../data/accounting-master/events.jsonl)\\n- [Active manifest]\\nP01 keys ['schema_version', 'status', 'record_count', 'input_hashes', 'records', 'mission_complete', 'residuals']\\nfirst record {'document_id': 'apple-2018-annual', 'issuer_id': 'apple', 'period_year': 2018, 'report_class': 'annual', 'region': 'United States', 'industry': 'technology hardware and services', 'stated_basis_family': 'us_gaap', 'source_url': 'https://www.annualreports.com/HostedData/AnnualReportArchive/a/NASDAQ_AAPL_2018.pdf', 'original_path': 'data/financial-report-benchmark/documents/apple/apple-2018-annual/original.pdf', 'original_sha256': 'f6c952c28c2eebcedfa1c484eacca649822bbcff025d5934d3da72def8a3f7ff', 'extracted_path': 'data/financial-report-benchmark/documents/apple/apple-2018-annual/extracted-93c1137880699fb55e83b05e8ac49c83ef9b3ba2bf4da577cac281b04cff5b4d.txt', 'extracted_sha256': '93c1137880699fb55e83b05e8ac49c83ef9b3ba2bf4da577cac281b04cff5b4d', 'basis_evidence': [{'match_text_offset': 141095, 'pattern': '(?:financial statements|financial report|reported results|财务报表|財務報表|财务报告).{0,300}?(?:prepar|accordance|conform|按照|根据|编制|編製|遵循|符合).{0,250}?(?:u\\\\\\\\.?s\\\\\\\\.?\\\\\\\\s+generally accepted accounting principles)', 'quote': 'itical Accounting Policies and Estimates The preparation of financial statements and related disclosures in conformity with U.S. generally accepted accounting principles (“GAAP”) and the Company’s discussion and analysis of its financial condition and operating results requ\\ninventories [('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P06/execution-0/pre-edit-files.json', 47967), ('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P06/execution-1/pre-edit-files.json', 48912)]\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_21\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"rg -n 'context|Reading|domain|publication|uncertainty' scripts/core0_ir_v