ed; broader transformations/policies are explicitly unsupported.')\\np.write_text(s)\\np=Path('docs/design/spec/context-chronology-profile-v1.md');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('MC02/MC05: context and partition checks; MC06/MC07: chronology and YTD revision\\\\\\\\nselection; MC10: category admission; MC11/MC14: query-dependent grouping and\\\\\\\\napproximation.', 'MC02: numeric context; MC05: chronology and YTD; MC06: perimeter rejection;\\\\\\\\nMC07: mappings and partitions; MC10: category admission; MC11: query-dependent\\\\\\\\ngrouping and approximation; MC14: information dates and scenario semantics.')\\ns+='''\\n## Repair audit and executable scope\\n\\nThe recovery audit rejected field-presence checks as evidence of semantic admission.\\nIt also found that selected source values did not drive the integrated calculation.\\nThe repaired tests use independent rational/set oracles, reference resolution,\\ncutoff boundaries, invalid inputs and source-value/revision-link mutations.\\nA failing invariant requires repair; missing provenance, changed protected inputs,\\nor invalid test execution prevents a passing report. No ranking or scientific\\nexperiment is performed. Conformance and result files preserve actual checks.\\n\\nContext records require explicit Gregorian calendars and immutable dimensions.\\nComponent and reclassification operations enumerate atomic population values with\\none contribution per member. Combining two complete axes over the same population\\nis rejected. Identity harmonisation creates a new observation with the original\\nvalue, source and dependency; all numerical harmonisations are unsupported.\\nUnknown retained-byte availability is visible as unresolved and excluded by the\\nintegrated entrypoint. Low-level selection defaults to assertion chronology;\\n\\\"'`require_known_bytes=True` requests the stricter historical-byte view.\\n\\nAdmission resolves source/locator, accepted evidence, dated package permission and\\neligibility, finite historical domains and evidence bounds, measurement input\\navailability and method-specific inputs, dated policy information and complete\\nfinite joint laws. Supported estimate operations are direct/observable values and\\nsingle-cash-flow DCF with integer nonnegative years. Only a hold behaviour policy\\nis implemented. These restrictions are explicit rejection boundaries, not general\\naccounting defaults. Permissions and evidence assertions still require substantive\\nreview; structural acceptance cannot establish their truth.\\n\\nFixed-rate debt uses exact principal-times-rate-times-horizon simple accrual. The\\nhorizon is an explicitly supplied year fraction; no inherited day count is used.\\nMaturity at or before the horizon, floating resets and hedges are unsupported.\\nFresh grouping checks run after horizon, scenario, report or evidence changes.\\nCached signatures include actual constituent values. The triangle bound follows\\nfrom |T sum P_i(r_i-r*)| <= T sum P_i|r_i-r*| for P_i,T >= 0; it is recomputed\\non every approximation request. A supplied signature must match; absent signatures\\nrequest fresh certification, not reuse of prior error evidence. Exact outputs and\\napproximate estimates are separately labelled.\\n\\nThe finite synthetic amounts and permissions are convenience inputs justified by\\ntransparent arithmetic and controlled rejection cases. Their failure mode is a\\nshared interpretation error; source and professional accounting validity remain\\nunevaluated. P01 adapter preserves publication metadata without promoting filing\\ndates to retained-byte availability. P03 adapters preserve literal/review metadata\\nand require missing context supplements explicitly. Returned results are copied\\nfrom engine state, and failed mutations are atomic.\\n'\\\"''';p.write_text(s)\\nprint('Corrected test fixture, requirement coverage, checker probes and bounded profile.')\\nPY\\npython3 -B /tmp/p06_checker.py\\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python3