{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06/progress.md; nl -ba docs/design/spec/context-chronology-profile-v1.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# P06 repair progress\n     2\t\n     3\tRecovery verified: all eight phase files exist; the prior process timed out despite a worker-authored passing report. The approved plan and execution inventories are present. No independent result acceptance exists.\n     4\t\n     5\tSkeptical audit found material omissions in the recovered candidate: component mappings lacked membership semantics; harmonisation only recorded metadata; supersession selection missed transitive unavailable intermediates; uncertainty categories mostly checked field presence; source evidence did not drive integrated derivation; grouping reuse was not bound to constituent data. Existing passing probes are insufficient for the approved criteria.\n     6\t\n     7\tRepair scope: only the existing P06 runtime, profile, fixture, tests, checker and declared outputs. Preserve all protected inputs and prior snapshots. Exact Fraction arithmetic, finite populations, Gregorian intervals and fixed unhedged bullet debt remain bounded assumptions. No scientific experiment or default promotion is being run.\n     8\t\n     9\tNext checks: add semantic negative and input-sensitivity cases; run P06/P03/P04 unittest discovery with CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1; regenerate checker results with approved-plan.json and execution-1/pre-edit-files.json; verify failed-check exit and source/protection hashes. Remaining deliverables: repaired conformance.json and result.md with honest scope limits, then independent result review.\n     1\t# Context, chronology, and resolution profile v1\n     2\t\n     3\tThis bounded profile implements P06 engineering behaviour for exact rational\n     4\tquantities, Gregorian half-open dates, finite populations, and nonnegative\n     5\tunhedged bullet debt. It is a versioned runtime contract, not an accounting\n     6\teligibility or forecast-validity claim.\n     7\t\n     8\t## Public operations\n     9\t\n    10\t`Context` identifies concept, entity, perimeter and version, basis, measurement,\n    11\tunit/currency, calendar, dimensions, and gross/net status. `compatible_context`\n    12\trequires all fields to match or an explicit dated `MappingRule`; parent/group,\n    13\tperimeter, basis, measurement, currency, calendar, dimension, and gross/net\n    14\tmismatches are rejected. Mapping cycles, expired rules, and unsupported conversion\n    15\tkinds fail with stable diagnostic codes.\n    16\t\n    17\t`check_partition` independently checks finite member sets. Members must be disjoint\n    18\tand cover the declared population, or an explicitly named residual must be present;\n    19\tan unknown residual cannot produce an exact total. Population and axis signatures\n    20\tprevent combining alternative classifications.\n    21\t\n    22\t`select_evidence` validates a supersession DAG and filters assertions by filing\n    23\tavailability and optional ingestion cutoff before selecting `original`,\n    24\t`latest_available`, or `harmonised`. Date-only availability requires an explicit\n    25\tnamed timezone and `next_local_midnight` policy. Unknown retained-byte vintage is\n    26\treturned as unresolved. Harmonisation preserves source IDs and transformation\n    27\tprovenance.\n    28\t\n    29\t`subtract_cumulative` computes an exact scalar flow only when concept, context,\n    30\tcalendar, start, nested exclusive ends, and revision compatibility agree. It\n    31\trejects instant values and incompatible vintages; reviewed exceptions must name\n    32\tscope and evidence.\n    33\t\n    34\t`admit_uncertainty` supports exactly six categories: ExtractionReading,\n    35\tHistoricalFact, AccountingElection, MeasurementEstimate, BehaviourPolicy, and\n    36\tFutureInnovation. It validates dependencies and category-specific fields. Unknown\n    37\tcategories, unsupported methods/treatments, invalid finite joint laws, and\n    38\tincompatible measures fail explicitly.\n    39\t\n    40\t`resolve_bullet_debt` retains constituents and validates a query signature over\n    41\tcontract, context, evidence view, horizon, scenario, requested outputs, and accrual\n    42\tconvention. Any changed signature requires fresh validation. The supported exact\n    43\tcase is fixed-rate unhedged bullet debt with no maturity crossing. The optional\n    44\tfixed-rate approximation requires nonnegative horizon, a declared tolerance, and a\n    45\tcertificate using the triangle inequality:\n    46\t`|sum(P_i r_i T)-sum(P_i) r* T| <= T sum(P_i |r_i-r*|)`.\n    47\t\n    48\t## Evidence and default audit\n    49\t\n    50\t| Choice | Provenance | Failure mode | Smallest diagnostic | Status |\n    51\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n    52\t| Exact `Fraction` arithmetic | Core 0 and P03 rational helpers | float rounding changes subtraction or bounds | independent Fraction oracle | reviewed bounded default |\n    53\t| Gregorian half-open dates | Core 0 temporal fixture | inclusive end or calendar mismatch | nested interval tests | reviewed bounded default |\n    54\t| Date-only next-local-midnight | approved P06 plan | UTC/local boundary selects wrong assertion | named-zone boundary test | explicit policy |\n    55\t| Finite partition populations | approved P06 plan | proof string hides overlap or omission | set enumeration | convenience test input |\n    56\t| Six uncertainty categories | P03 admission fields and approved plan | malformed evidence admitted | positive plus semantic negative per category | bounded support |\n    57\t| Bullet-debt grouping | P04 additive reference and approved plan | stale/query-insufficient grouping | query signature and constituent oracle | bounded hypothesis |\n    58\t| Approximation certificate | approved plan derivation | tolerance claimed without error bound | exact difference versus bound | optional reviewed path |\n    59\t\n    60\tSynthetic fixtures test structure only. P01 source records with\n    61\t`historical_byte_vintage=not_established_by_this_inventory` remain unresolved for\n    62\thistorical byte selection. Passing this profile does not establish professional\n    63\taccounting treatment, empirical forecast validity, or human acceptance.\n    64\t\n    65\t## Criterion map\n    66\t\n    67\tMC02: numeric context; MC05: chronology and YTD; MC06: perimeter rejection;\n    68\tMC07: mappings and partitions; MC10: category admission; MC11: query-dependent\n    69\tgrouping and approximation; MC14: information dates and scenario semantics. Tests in `tests/test_accounting_p06.py` provide independent expected\n    70\tsets and arithmetic.\n    71\t\n    72\t## Repair audit and executable scope\n    73\t\n    74\tThe recovery audit rejected field-presence checks as evidence of semantic admission.\n    75\tIt also found that selected source values did not drive the integrated calculation.\n    76\tThe repaired tests use independent rational/set oracles, reference resolution,\n    77\tcutoff boundaries, invalid inputs and source-value/revision-link mutations.\n    78\tA failing invariant requires repair; missing provenance, changed protected inputs,\n    79\tor invalid test execution prevents a passing report. No ranking or scientific\n    80\texperiment is performed. Conformance and result files preserve actual checks.\n    81\t\n    82\tContext records require explicit Gregorian calendars and immutable dimensions.\n    83\tComponent and reclassification operations enumerate atomic population values with\n    84\tone contribution per member. Combining two complete axes over the same population\n    85\tis rejected. Identity harmonisation creates a new observation with the original\n    86\tvalue, source and dependency; all numerical harmonisations are unsupported.\n    87\tUnknown retained-byte availability is visible as unresolved and excluded by the\n    88\tintegrated entrypoint. Low-level selection defaults to assertion chronology;\n    89\t`require_known_bytes=True` requests the stricter historical-byte view.\n    90\t\n    91\tAdmission resolves source/locator, accepted evidence, dated package permission and\n    92\teligibility, finite historical domains and evidence bounds, measurement input\n    93\tavailability and method-specific inputs, dated policy information and complete\n    94\tfinite joint laws. Supported estimate operations are direct/observable values and\n    95\tsingle-cash-flow DCF with integer nonnegative years. Only a hold behaviour policy\n    96\tis implemented. These restrictions are explicit rejection boundaries, not general\n    97\taccounting defaults. Permissions and evidence assertions still require substantive\n    98\treview; structural acceptance cannot establish their truth.\n    99\t\n   100\tFixed-rate debt uses exact principal-times-rate-times-horizon simple accrual. The\n   101\thorizon is an explicitly supplied year fraction; no inherited day count is used.\n   102\tMaturity at or before the horizon, floating resets and hedges are unsupported.\n   103\tFresh grouping checks run after horizon, scenario, report or evidence changes.\n   104\tCached signatures include actual constituent values. The triangle bound follows\n   105\tfrom |T sum P_i(r_i-r*)| <= T sum P_i|r_i-r*| for P_i,T >= 0; it is recomputed\n   106\ton every approximation request. A supplied signature must match; absent signatures\n   107\trequest fresh certification, not reuse of prior error evidence. Exact outputs and\n   108\tapproximate estimates are separately labelled.\n   109\t\n   110\tThe finite synthetic amounts and permissions are convenience inputs justified by\n   111\ttransparent arithmetic and controlled rejection cases. Their failure mode is a\n   112\tshared interpretation error; source and professional accounting validity remain\n   113\tunevaluated. P01 adapter preserves publication metadata without promoting filing\n   114\tdates to retained-byte availability. P03 adapters preserve literal/review metadata\n   115\tand require missing context supplements explicitly. Returned results are copied\n   116\tfrom engine state, and failed mutations are atomic.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba scripts/context_chronology_v1.py | sed -n '670,840p'\"","aggregated_output":"   670\t        if any(record[\"driver\"] not in a[\"hypothesis\"] for a in record[\"joint_law\"][\"atoms\"]):\n   671\t            fail(\"INVALID_JOINT_LAW\", \"driver missing from joint atom\")\n   672\t        for dep in record[\"dependencies\"]:\n   673\t            if known_records[dep].get(\"measure\", record[\"measure\"]) != record[\"measure\"]:\n   674\t                fail(\"INCOMPATIBLE_PROBABILITY_MEASURE\", \"dependency measure differs\")\n   675\t    return deepcopy(record)\n   676\t\n   677\t\n   678\tdef guard_information_view(view: Mapping[str, Any], *, event_time: str | date, request: str = \"exogenous_stress\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n   679\t    if request != \"exogenous_stress\":\n   680\t        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_INFORMATION_OPERATION\", request, \"information_view\")\n   681\t    visible = set(view.get(\"visible\", ()))\n   682\t    announced = set(view.get(\"future_announced\", ()))\n   683\t    hidden = set(view.get(\"future_realised\", ()))\n   684\t    if hidden & visible or any(str(x).startswith(\"future_realised:\") for x in visible):\n   685\t        fail(\"FUTURE_INFORMATION_LEAKAGE\", \"future realised outcomes cannot be visible\")\n   686\t    when = _iso_date(event_time, \"event_time\") if isinstance(event_time, str) else event_time\n   687\t    records = view.get(\"records\", {})\n   688\t    for identifier in visible | announced:\n   689\t        row = records.get(identifier)\n   690\t        if row is None:\n   691\t            fail(\"UNRESOLVED_INFORMATION\", identifier)\n   692\t        if _iso_date(row[\"available_date\"], \"information.available_date\") > when:\n   693\t            fail(\"FUTURE_INFORMATION_LEAKAGE\", identifier)\n   694\t        future = _iso_date(row[\"event_date\"], \"information.event_date\") > when\n   695\t        if row.get(\"information_kind\") == \"future_realised\" or (future and (identifier not in announced or row.get(\"information_kind\") != \"announced_stress\")):\n   696\t            fail(\"FUTURE_INFORMATION_LEAKAGE\", identifier)\n   697\t    if not view.get(\"measure_id\"):\n   698\t        fail(\"MISSING_PROBABILITY_MEASURE\", \"information view needs a measure\")\n   699\t    if view.get(\"pricing_measure_id\") == view[\"measure_id\"]:\n   700\t        fail(\"INCOMPATIBLE_PROBABILITY_MEASURE\", \"pricing and real-world IDs must differ\")\n   701\t    return {\"status\": \"accepted\", \"event_time\": str(event_time), \"visible\": sorted(visible),\n   702\t            \"future_announced\": sorted(announced), \"future_realised_hidden\": sorted(hidden),\n   703\t            \"measure_id\": view[\"measure_id\"], \"selection_changes_history\": False}\n   704\t\n   705\t\n   706\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n   707\tclass DebtConstituent:\n   708\t    id: str\n   709\t    principal: Fraction\n   710\t    rate: Fraction\n   711\t    maturity: Fraction\n   712\t    reset: str = \"fixed\"\n   713\t    hedge: str = \"unhedged\"\n   714\t\n   715\t    def __post_init__(self):\n   716\t        for key in (\"principal\", \"rate\", \"maturity\"):\n   717\t            object.__setattr__(self, key, _fraction(getattr(self, key), key))\n   718\t        if self.principal < 0:\n   719\t            fail(\"NEGATIVE_PRINCIPAL\", self.id)\n   720\t        if self.maturity <= 0 or not self.id:\n   721\t            fail(\"INVALID_DEBT\", \"positive maturity and ID required\")\n   722\t\n   723\t    @classmethod\n   724\t    def from_dict(cls, row: Mapping[str, Any]) -> \"DebtConstituent\":\n   725\t        principal = _fraction(row.get(\"principal\"), f\"{row.get('id')}.principal\")\n   726\t        if principal < 0:\n   727\t            fail(\"NEGATIVE_PRINCIPAL\", \"principal must be nonnegative\", str(row.get(\"id\")))\n   728\t        return cls(str(row[\"id\"]), principal, _fraction(row.get(\"rate\"), f\"{row.get('id')}.rate\"),\n   729\t                   _fraction(row.get(\"maturity\"), f\"{row.get('id')}.maturity\"), str(row.get(\"reset\", \"fixed\")), str(row.get(\"hedge\", \"unhedged\")))\n   730\t\n   731\t\n   732\tdef _query_signature(query: Mapping[str, Any]) -> str:\n   733\t    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(query, sort_keys=True, default=str, separators=(\",\", \":\")).encode()).hexdigest()\n   734\t\n   735\t\n   736\tdef interest_certificate(constituents: Sequence[DebtConstituent], target_rate: Fraction | str | int,\n   737\t                         horizon: Fraction | str | int) -> dict[str, Fraction]:\n   738\t    T = _fraction(horizon, \"horizon\")\n   739\t    if T < 0:\n   740\t        fail(\"INVALID_HORIZON\", \"horizon must be nonnegative\", \"horizon\")\n   741\t    rstar = _fraction(target_rate, \"target_rate\")\n   742\t    exact = sum((c.principal * c.rate * T for c in constituents), Fraction())\n   743\t    approx = sum((c.principal * rstar * T for c in constituents), Fraction())\n   744\t    bound = T * sum((c.principal * abs(c.rate - rstar) for c in constituents), Fraction())\n   745\t    difference = abs(exact - approx)\n   746\t    if difference > bound:\n   747\t        fail(\"INVALID_APPROXIMATION_CERTIFICATE\", \"triangle-inequality bound is violated\", \"approximation\")\n   748\t    return {\"exact\": exact, \"approximate\": approx, \"error\": difference, \"bound\": bound}\n   749\t\n   750\t\n   751\tdef resolve_bullet_debt(constituents: Sequence[DebtConstituent | Mapping[str, Any]], query: Mapping[str, Any], *,\n   752\t                       previous: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None,\n   753\t                       approximation: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n   754\t    rows = [x if isinstance(x, DebtConstituent) else DebtConstituent.from_dict(x) for x in constituents]\n   755\t    if not rows:\n   756\t        fail(\"EMPTY_DEBT_SET\", \"at least one constituent is required\", \"debt\")\n   757\t    required = (\"contract\", \"context\", \"evidence_view\", \"horizon\", \"scenario\", \"requested_outputs\", \"accrual_convention\", \"group_by\")\n   758\t    for key in required:\n   759\t        if key not in query:\n   760\t            fail(\"MISSING_QUERY_FIELD\", f\"missing {key}\", \"query\")\n   761\t    if len({c.id for c in rows}) != len(rows):\n   762\t        fail(\"DUPLICATE_CONSTITUENT\", \"debt IDs must be unique\")\n   763\t    signature = _query_signature({\"query\": query, \"constituents\": [vars(c) for c in rows]})\n   764\t    if previous is not None and previous.get(\"query_signature\") != signature:\n   765\t        fail(\"STALE_RESULT\", \"query changed; grouping sufficiency must be revalidated\", \"query\")\n   766\t    horizon = _fraction(query[\"horizon\"], \"query.horizon\")\n   767\t    if horizon < 0:\n   768\t        fail(\"INVALID_HORIZON\", \"horizon must be nonnegative\", \"query.horizon\")\n   769\t    if query[\"scenario\"] not in {\"base\", \"announced_stress\"}:\n   770\t        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_SCENARIO\", str(query[\"scenario\"]), \"query.scenario\")\n   771\t    if query[\"accrual_convention\"] != \"simple_actual_fraction\":\n   772\t        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_ACCRUAL\", str(query[\"accrual_convention\"]), \"query.accrual_convention\")\n   773\t    if not isinstance(query[\"requested_outputs\"], list) or not query[\"requested_outputs\"]:\n   774\t        fail(\"MISSING_OUTPUT_REQUEST\", \"requested_outputs must be nonempty\", \"query\")\n   775\t    unsupported_outputs = set(query[\"requested_outputs\"]) - {\"interest\", \"principal\"}\n   776\t    if unsupported_outputs:\n   777\t        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_OUTPUT\", f\"unsupported outputs: {sorted(unsupported_outputs)}\", \"query.requested_outputs\")\n   778\t    dimensions = (\"rate\", \"maturity\", \"reset\", \"hedge\")\n   779\t    group_by = set(query[\"group_by\"])\n   780\t    if not group_by <= set(dimensions):\n   781\t        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_GROUP_DIMENSION\", \"group_by contains unsupported dimension\", \"query.group_by\")\n   782\t    for dim in dimensions:\n   783\t        values = {getattr(c, dim) for c in rows}\n   784\t        if len(values) > 1 and dim not in group_by:\n   785\t            fail(\"GROUPING_INSUFFICIENT\", f\"dimension {dim} varies but is not grouped\", \"query.group_by\")\n   786\t    for c in rows:\n   787\t        if c.hedge != \"unhedged\":\n   788\t            fail(\"HEDGED_DEBT_UNSUPPORTED\", \"only unhedged debt is supported\", c.id)\n   789\t        if c.reset != \"fixed\":\n   790\t            fail(\"RESET_UNSUPPORTED\", \"only fixed reset is supported\", c.id)\n   791\t        if c.maturity <= horizon:\n   792\t            fail(\"MATURITY_CROSSING\", \"maturity crosses the requested horizon\", c.id)\n   793\t    groups: dict[tuple[Any, ...], list[DebtConstituent]] = {}\n   794\t    for c in rows:\n   795\t        key = tuple(getattr(c, dim) if dim in group_by else \"homogeneous\" for dim in dimensions)\n   796\t        groups.setdefault(key, []).append(c)\n   797\t    output: dict[str, Any] = {}\n   798\t    if \"interest\" in query[\"requested_outputs\"]:\n   799\t        output[\"interest\"] = sum((c.principal * c.rate * horizon for c in rows), Fraction())\n   800\t    if \"principal\" in query[\"requested_outputs\"]:\n   801\t        output[\"principal\"] = sum((c.principal for c in rows), Fraction())\n   802\t    result = {\"status\": \"resolved\", \"query_signature\": signature,\n   803\t              \"query\": json.loads(json.dumps(query, default=str)), \"groups\": [\n   804\t                  {\"key\": [str(x) for x in key], \"constituent_ids\": [c.id for c in members],\n   805\t                   \"principal\": sum((c.principal for c in members), Fraction()),\n   806\t                   \"interest\": sum((c.principal * c.rate * horizon for c in members), Fraction())}\n   807\t                  for key, members in groups.items()],\n   808\t              \"outputs\": output, \"constituent_ids\": [c.id for c in rows], \"constituents\": deepcopy(rows), \"fresh\": True}\n   809\t    if approximation is not None:\n   810\t        if not approximation.get(\"scope\") or approximation.get(\"scope\") != \"fixed_rate_interest\" or not approximation.get(\"evidence\"):\n   811\t            fail(\"APPROXIMATION_EVIDENCE_REQUIRED\", \"declared scope and evidence are required\", \"approximation\")\n   812\t        if approximation.get(\"query_signature\", signature) != signature:\n   813\t            fail(\"STALE_APPROXIMATION\", \"error evidence is for different query/constituents\")\n   814\t        cert = interest_certificate(rows, approximation.get(\"target_rate\"), horizon)\n   815\t        tolerance = _fraction(approximation.get(\"tolerance\"), \"approximation.tolerance\")\n   816\t        declared = _fraction(approximation.get(\"error_bound\"), \"approximation.error_bound\")\n   817\t        if tolerance < 0 or declared < cert[\"error\"] or declared > tolerance or declared < cert[\"bound\"]:\n   818\t            fail(\"APPROXIMATION_BOUND_INVALID\", \"declared bound must cover exact error and certificate within tolerance\", \"approximation\")\n   819\t        result[\"approximation\"] = {k: str(v) for k, v in cert.items()} | {\"tolerance\": str(tolerance), \"declared_error_bound\": str(declared), \"query_signature\": signature, \"evidence\": deepcopy(approximation[\"evidence\"])}\n   820\t    return result\n   821\t\n   822\t\n   823\tdef adapt_core_context(row: Mapping[str, Any], *, perimeter_version: str, gross_net: str,\n   824\t                       calendar: str, display: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None) -> Context:\n   825\t    \"\"\"Core 0 omits perimeter version/gross-net; require explicit supplements.\"\"\"\n   826\t    dimensions = row.get(\"dimensions\", [])\n   827\t    if len({d[\"axis\"] for d in dimensions}) != len(dimensions):\n   828\t        fail(\"INVALID_DIMENSIONS\", \"duplicate Core 0 axis\")\n   829\t    return Context.from_dict({k: row[k] for k in (\"concept\", \"entity\", \"perimeter\", \"basis\", \"measurement\", \"unit\", \"currency\")} |\n   830\t                             {\"perimeter_version\": perimeter_version, \"gross_net\": gross_net,\n   831\t                              \"calendar\": calendar, \"dimensions\": {d[\"axis\"]: d[\"member\"] for d in dimensions}} | dict(display or {}))\n   832\t\n   833\t\n   834\tdef adapt_p03_reading(binding: Any, context: Context, *, historical_byte_vintage: str = \"unknown\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n   835\t    if binding.currency != context.currency:\n   836\t        fail(\"CURRENCY_MISMATCH\", \"reading and context differ\")\n   837\t    return {\"id\": binding.key, \"kind\": \"instant\", \"amount\": _fraction(binding.amount),\n   838\t            \"concept\": context.concept, \"context\": context.as_dict(), \"calendar\": context.calendar,\n   839\t            \"period\": {\"start\": binding.instant, \"end\": None}, \"available\": binding.available,\n   840\t            \"ingested\": binding.ingested, \"source\": binding.filing_id, \"supersedes\": [],\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
